Z||000011||Cheever2||10-01-2000||02:09 AM||||I don't like it.  The nose doesn't seem to match the rest of the car.  Photo looks authentic to me.  I do like the wheels & tires.  Maybe if I saw it in person I'd like it better.<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000012||Monkeyman||10-01-2000||08:25 AM||||Hard to tell from the pic, but it almost looks like the fenders are part of the fascia/air dam, too.  Nice look, but it really would be a b**** if it got wrecked.  Although I suppose, with the right insurance, it wouldn't matter.  Let Allstate pay to have it redone (by someone else, of course).||||reg||1
Z||000013||fropuff||10-01-2000||10:23 AM||||I think Monkeyman's right.  The front looks as if it's all in one piece.  A big piece.  I was looking at it too, and I also think the surrounding things look fake.  Even the guy at the car next to it does.  Oh well.  At least the car looks real.  The only thing I think I would have done is leave the "seam" between the fascia and the ground effects.  That way, the front fascia can be a "separate" piece, and then the ground effects and the chin spoiler can be all "one" piece.  I think I would have left the front separate from the fenders.  That way, the original lines would be the same, but the GFX and the chin spoiler would be in one piece.  I like it this way, but probably better the other way!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Oreif||10-01-2000||01:41 PM||||The top definately looks chopped. If your interested in chopping the top of your car, I'm sure Archie can help. He built a blue GT and chopped the top. The nice thing is he uses the original windsheild. I think his chop is 3".<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
